  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OEGI - Kenya County Small Business Centers Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kenya):  Using FY 2022 Feed the Future funds, USAID will continue its support for the Kenya Small Business Development Centers (SBDC) activity to strengthen Kenya&apos;s private sector competitiveness and enhance its prospects for sustained growth by increasing the quality, quantity and sustainability of Kenya&apos;s SBDCs.  The activity will work to establish a network of six SBDCs, which will provide an array of services to micro and small businesses, including; business advisory services, trade and market information, facilitating access to finance, and sharing policy innovations.  This will increase the productivity and profitability of micro and small businesses through tailored advisory and consulting services and catalyze the growth and competitiveness in the domestic, regional and international markets..The activity will also help the Kenyan private sector advocate for a conducive business environment by supporting sectoral Business Associations (BAs) which will advocate for their members. These BAs will focus on analyzing and advocating for an enabling business and investment environment on behalf of their members through Public-Private Dialogue. .The activity will also support agriculture Business Associations (BAs) at the county and national levels with a focus on market systems strengthening and producing value addition.  Specifically, the activity will enhance the BAs&apos; capacity to analyze policies and advocate for a positive business environment. By strengthening BAs&apos;management capacity, technical skills, resource mobilization, member participation, and external engagement ability, USAID will also enable BA members to be vibrant and competitive by increasing investments, creating jobs, and growing businesses that can create jobs and reduce poverty.. ..</narrative>
  </description>
